{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Pushed — Gerrit change [3125](https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/3125), awaiting votes (2026-10-27 ~23:55 PDT)\n\nCommit `5775f968a90`, hashtag `rebar-session-c657653d`. Two files, 102 insertions / 14 deletions: `pyproject.toml` and `tests/unit/test_packaging_dependencies.py`. Votes not yet cast at push time.\n\n### `make verify` result — read this before closing\n\n`make verify` ran to completion (1 h 31 m, `PYTEST_WORKERS=4`) and **exited 2: 22 failed, 19,835 passed, 88 skipped, 1 error**.\n\n**None of the 22 failures is caused by this change, and none can be.** They are all in `tests/scripts/test_observability_*` (`..._mcp_health_9ea3.py`, `..._offsets_6a65.py`, `..._marker_anchor_8c2f.py`, `..._mcp_markers.py`), which drive `infra/scripts/observability.sh`. This commit touches `pyproject.toml`'s sdist `include`/`exclude` and one file under `tests/unit/` — `git diff --name-only` on the commit confirms it reaches neither `infra/` nor `tests/scripts/`.\n\nThe failure is a host-environment gap, captured verbatim in the log:\n\n```\nobservability.sh: line 160: /var/lib/rebar/probe-region: No such file or directory\nobservability.sh: line 230: /var/lib/rebar/reviewbot-webhook-auth-offset: No such file or directory\nsubprocess.TimeoutExpired: Command '['bash', '.../infra/scripts/observability.sh']'\n  timed out after 59.99996245803777 seconds\n```\n\n`/var/lib/rebar/` does not exist on this macOS host, the script's writes fail, and it then runs past the test's own 60 s subprocess bound. Filed separately rather than absorbed here.\n\n### What was actually verified for this change\n\n- `make lint` — clean (ruff check + format-check, complexity/mechanism ratchets, zizmor, actionlint).\n- `make typecheck` — `mypy`: no issues in 749 source files.\n- `tests/unit/test_packaging_dependencies.py` — 9 passed, including both new tests.\n- Red-then-green demonstrated by restoring the bare `\"README.md\"`: the new sdist test fails naming `.github`, `examples`, `scripts`.\n- The 19,835 passing tests include every other unit test in the suite.\n\nCI on `ubuntu-latest` is the authoritative `Verified` signal and is unaffected by the macOS-only gap above.\n\n### Before closing\n\nDo not close until change 3125 is `Verified +1` and merged. At that point set `file_impact` to `pyproject.toml` and `tests/unit/test_packaging_dependencies.py` and re-run `review_plan_start` — declaring file impact is a material edit that stales the current PASS attestation, which is why it was deliberately left until close (see the previous comment)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793169255000506684,"uuid":"715cdc2e-95b2-494e-a205-2771e0bb6c84"}